
### restack replays descendants onto the updated parent
$ git stack restack
restacking stack rooted at feat-a
restacking feat-b onto feat-a
done.
[exit 0]
feat-b behind feat-a: 0
feat-b contains a2: 1
HEAD: feat-b

### restack aborts cleanly on a conflict
$ git stack restack
restacking stack rooted at feat-a
restacking feat-b onto feat-a
error: conflict while rebasing 'feat-b' onto 'feat-a'.
Resolve it manually with:
    git checkout feat-b && git rebase feat-a
then re-run 'git stack restack'.
[exit 1]
rebase in progress: 0

### restack leaves an untracked branch alone
$ git stack restack
restacking stack rooted at feat-a
done.
[exit 0]
HEAD: feat-a

### restack falls back to merge-base when stackBase is unrecorded
$ git stack restack
restacking stack rooted at feat-a
restacking feat-b onto feat-a
'feat-b': no recorded stack base; rebasing onto 'feat-a'
done.
[exit 0]
feat-b behind feat-a: 0
feat-b commits above feat-a: 1
feat-b contains a2: 1
feat-b contains b1: 1
feat-b stackBase == feat-a tip (re-recorded): yes

### restack skips a rewritten parent's old copies when stackBase is not in the branch
$ git stack restack
restacking stack rooted at feat-a
restacking feat-b onto feat-a
'feat-b': stack base 3635e3f3668ac98adba4c7fd497e93020994995c is not in its history; rebasing onto 'feat-a'
done.
[exit 0]
feat-b behind feat-a: 0
feat-b commits above feat-a: 1
feat-b contains b1: 1

### restack skips a rewritten parent's old copies when stackBase is unrecorded
$ git stack restack
restacking stack rooted at feat-a
restacking feat-b onto feat-a
'feat-b': no recorded stack base; rebasing onto 'feat-a'
done.
[exit 0]
feat-b behind feat-a: 0
feat-b commits above feat-a: 1
feat-b contains b1: 1
